I drink my water.
My glass is now empty.
I would like to go now.
I am still sitting comfortably at my table.
I see the waiter.
I raise my hand.
The waiter comes over to me.
“Would you like anything else?” he asks.
“No, thank you,” I say politely.
“Could I pay, please?” I ask.
“Of course,” he answers.
He is standing right at my table.
He has a small wallet in his hand.
It is made of leather.
He opens the wallet.
I get my money.
